{"name":"Sphere","hex":"#f2e8cc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sphere","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A surface in three dimensions consisting of all points equidistant from a center. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}.","An object which appears to be bounded by a sphere; a round object, a ball."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place in a sphere, or among the spheres; to ensphere.","To make round or spherical; to perfect."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sphere"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sphere","blocks":[{"text":"A sphere is a surface analogous to the circle, a curve. In solid geometry, a sphere is the set of points that are all at the same distance r from a given point in three-dimensional space. That given point is the center of the sphere, and the distance r is the sphere's radius. The earliest known mentions of spheres appear in the work of the ancient Greek mathematicians."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Sphere_wireframe_10deg_6r.svg/330px-Sphere_wireframe_10deg_6r.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sphere"},{"title":"Sphere (venue)","blocks":[{"text":"Sphere is a music and entertainment arena in Paradise, Nevada, United States, east of the Las Vegas Strip. Designed by Populous, the project was announced by the Madison Square Garden Company in 2018, known then as the MSG Sphere. The venue, which seats 17,600 people and has total capacity of 20,000, is being marketed for its immersive video and audio capabilities, which include a 16K resolution wraparound interior LED screen, speakers with beamforming and wave field synthesis technologies, and 4D physical effects. The venue's exterior also features 580,000 sq ft (54,000 m2) of LED displays, making it the largest in the world. Sphere measures 366 feet (112 m) high and 516 feet (157 m) wide; it would be the largest spherical building on Earth, if it were not a geodesic dome. The arena cost $2.3 billion, making it the most expensive entertainment venue built in the Las Vegas Valley."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Sphere-exosphere-on-Jan-26-2024.jpg/330px-Sphere-exosphere-on-Jan-26-2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sphere_(venue)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Sphere_and_Ball.png/500px-Sphere_and_Ball.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Sphere_and_Ball.png/1280px-Sphere_and_Ball.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Sphere_and_Ball.png/500px-Sphere_and_Ball.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two orthogonal radii of a sphere","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASphere_and_Ball.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Sphere_section.png/330px-Sphere_section.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Sphere_section.png/330px-Sphere_section.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A normal vector to a sphere, a normal plane and its normal section. The curvature of the curve of intersection is the sectional curvature. For the sphere each normal section through a given point will be a circle of the same radius: the radius of the sphere. This means that every point on the sphere will be an umbilical point.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASphere_section.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Sphere_halve.png/500px-Sphere_halve.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Sphere_halve.png/500px-Sphere_halve.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Great circle on a sphere","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASphere_halve.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Loxodrome.png/500px-Loxodrome.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Loxodrome.png/500px-Loxodrome.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Loxodrome","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALoxodrome.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Einstein_gyro_gravity_probe_b.jpg/500px-Einstein_gyro_gravity_probe_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Einstein_gyro_gravity_probe_b.jpg/960px-Einstein_gyro_gravity_probe_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Einstein_gyro_gravity_probe_b.jpg/500px-Einstein_gyro_gravity_probe_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEinstein_gyro_gravity_probe_b.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/King_of_spades-_spheres.jpg/250px-King_of_spades-_spheres.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/King_of_spades-_spheres.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/King_of_spades-_spheres.jpg/250px-King_of_spades-_spheres.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u